  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user searching the forum, I want the query field to be the system search field (magnifier, clear button, a prompt that says what is searched), so that search looks and works as elsewhere on iOS.\n\n### Rule\n\n\"A search field is an editable text field that displays a Search icon, a Clear button, and placeholder text where people can enter what they are searching for.\" and \"Use placeholder text to help people know what they can search for.\" — [HIG › Search fields](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/search-fields) (page updated 2026-06-08).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n`App/SwiftHFR/Search/ForumSearchView.swift:59-64`: `TextField(\"Rechercher\", text: $model.text)….submitLabel(.search)` as a form row: no `.searchable`, no clear button, and a placeholder that is the verb alone.\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\nSame: `HFRswift/Swift/ForumSearchView.swift:167` `TextField(\"Rechercher\", text: $viewModel.params.searchText)`.\n\n### Class\n\n**(b) evolution, M5** (same as legacy).\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- Move the query to `.searchable(text:prompt:)` with a prompt such as « Sujets et messages du forum », keeping the form rows (category, period, author) as filters below. The smiley picker already uses `.searchable`; #880 asks the same for the GIF panel.\n- Mac check: the field shows the magnifier and the clear button; the pager still hides while the field has focus.\n\nRelated: #694 (unified search, M5: fold in if it already covers the field), #880.\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
